  "editorReview": {
    "text": "This history of handheld consoles shines when it grounds its 'Portability Trilemma' argument in the tangible physics of battery chemistry and manufacturing cost. The analysis of the Switch's 'software-defined sacrifice' is a standout example of the book's strength: using the device as a lens to dissect engineering philosophy. However, the central biographical promise falters. The compelling origin story of Gunpei Yokoi is front-loaded, but the text later abandons him as a living subject, failing to examine his later contradictions with the same material rigor. This structural lapse, alongside",
